nd parses stdout/exit codes","Sibling 9895/424f/4a44 (closed) built preview/sync as the reconciler engine invoked via launch_reconciler / python -m rebar_reconciler; the _Disposition type is defined at src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py, not as an importable in-process op","In-process cores exist for fsck (_engine_support.bridge_fsck.audit_bridge_mappings) but no equivalent importable preview/sync core is evident"],"finding":"The plan requires library/MCP adapters to 'not shell out through the CLI' and to translate the 9895 typed disposition once, but for preview/sync that typed disposition currently lives only at the reconciler engine's subprocess boundary (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py); the existing rebar.reconcile() shells out and there is no in-process preview/sync core function exposing the disposition. The plan does not name the in-process core seam the adapters will call.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52ae6a7f29d1966d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Shared implementation and error policy'; File impact 'src/rebar/_lib_ops.py'","norm_id":"n5ac814da72a771cc","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["Implementer wires bridge_preview()/bridge_sync() and, finding no in-process disposition entrypoint, either (a) shells out — violating the plan's explicit no-shell-out rule and re-deriving exit translation, or (b) has to design an unspecified in-process core seam mid-implementation, risking divergence from the CLI's disposition mapping.","MCP bridge_sync obtains a disposition inconsistently from the CLI path, breaking the 'translate once' guarantee."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In 'Shared implementation and error policy', specify the importable core function(s) (module + return type) that expose the preview/sync typed disposition in-process, confirm the CLI, library, and MCP all consume it, and clarify whether the legacy rebar.reconcile() subprocess launcher is refactore